# softmax.ckir - CEIR-24b the attention SCALED ROWWISE SOFTMAX kernel, GENERALIZED at CEIR-26d-3b to ANY Sk (the baked Sk=3 unroll
# retired): probs[r,c] = exp(scale*scores[r,c] - m_r) / SUM_c exp(scale*scores[r,c] - m_r), m_r = max_c(scale*scores[r,c]), the
# numerically-stable softmax; scale = 1/sqrt(D) rides as a CALLER-UPLOADED [1] buffer (scale@1). One lane per OUTPUT ROW r =
# LocalInvocationIndex in [0, Sq). ⛔ CEIR-26d-4e: local_size is the SENTINEL [0,1,1] = "bind Sq at cook" — the resolver cook-binds
# it to Sq=dim0(probs) via bind_authored_local_size (the relu.ckir sentinel mechanism; the EXTENT it supplies is Sq=rows, NOT numel),
# so an oversize Sq > kMaxAuthoredLocalSize (== the groupshared m_sh/d_sh cap 1024) is a TYPED LocalSizeExceedsLimit reject, not a
# silent device-illegal local_size (the OOB guard on the [1024] shared arrays is now EXPLICIT). Sk is a SPEC-CONSTANT (constant_id 0,
# default 3, U32 = node n6, axes=0x80000000) used as the loop bound of THREE uniform `For c in [0,Sk)` passes (max / exp-sum /
# normalize; exp RECOMPUTED in pass 3 -- no store-and-reload, the inline-load RAW scar). The per-row m_r/d_r are carried across the
# loop in GROUPSHARED slots (m_sh/d_sh, cap 1024 >= max Sq) -- kernel-tier For has NO register carry (CEIR-26d-3b-1); each lane
# touches only its own [r] slot => NO barrier. base = r*Sk is MATERIALIZED (stmt n7 leaf) at the body scope so all 3 loops share it
# (the temp-scope scar). ⛔ GENERATED by build_softmax (test_ckir_asset.cpp) via ckir_write -- REGEN with
# `crd-kir-tests.exe "[.emit-softmax]"` then RE-ADD this header (ckir_write emits a generic one). Node refs POSITIONAL; F32 default;
# LocalInvocationIndex = KBuiltin 4. 3 buffers: scores@0 (read) . scale@1 (read, [1]) . probs@2 (write). Verified device-free by
# test_ckir_viz.cpp "ceir 24b-2" (== CPU softmax at (2,3) AND (3,5)) + on-device by the 24b-4 + 26d-3c gates.
schema = 1

